<<<
 lour, lower. The meaning is frown. Spell lour & pronounce lowr. The word is not connected with low & the other verb lower (l0’er), & it is a pity that it should be confused with that verb by the second spelling (the oldest forms are lour & lure) & so
===


**lour, lower.** The meaning is frown. Spell *lour* & pronounce lowr. The word is not connected with *low* & the other verb *lower* (lō'er), & it is a pity that it should be confused with that verb by the second spelling (the oldest forms are *lour* & *lure*) & so
>>>

